From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shlomi Marco <s.marco@rubycomm.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: fix OTG state machine race during probe

During probe, extcon_set_state_sync() fires the rockchip_otg_event
notifier which schedules otg_sm_work with a 2-second delay. When
this work fires, if the PHY consumer (DWC3) has already called
phy_power_on(), the state machine may call phy_power_off() or
access stale regmap data, causing either a USB speed fallback to
full-speed (12Mbps) or a kernel panic in _regmap_bus_reg_write.

Fix by using extcon_set_state() instead of extcon_set_state_sync()
for the initial state sync during probe. This sets the cable state
for DWC3 to read via extcon_get_state() without firing notifiers
that schedule the premature work.

Signed-off-by: Shlomi Marco <s.marco@rubycomm.com>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -1359,7 +1359,7 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_otg_port_init(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy,
 		if (!of_property_present(rphy->dev->of_node, "extcon")) {
 			/* do initial sync of usb state */
 			id = property_enabled(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->utmi_id);
-			extcon_set_state_sync(rphy->edev, EXTCON_USB_HOST, !id);
+			extcon_set_state(rphy->edev, EXTCON_USB_HOST, !id);
 		}
 	}

